[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160863649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3160863649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3160863649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68ZvOh","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T16:43:30Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T16:43:43Z","body":"This might depend on which FileAccess mode is used to write the file (between `WRITE`, `READ_WRITE` and `WRITE_READ`).\n\nThat said, you can work around this by using \"shallow\" symlinks, where the parent folder is a symlink but the files are not. This is an approach recommended in many dotfile managers.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160863649/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160876252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3160876252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3160876252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68ZyTc","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T16:48:31Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T16:52:17Z","body":"How does other file editor deal with this? Is editing through a symlink expected to work generally?\n\nCan you test deactivating safe save? `filesystem/on_save/safe_save_on_backup_then_rename` editor setting, this copies and overwrites the file, which would be expected to overwrite it\n\nBut generally I think Godot just uses the OS systems for this, so unless other software writes specific functionality to handle writing *throuhg* symlinks they're likely to work the same way, assuming Godot does this when not safe saving","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160876252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160954762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3160954762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3160954762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68aFeK","user":{"login":"aliaslion","id":122117018,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0dbmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122117018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion","html_url":"https://github.com/aliaslion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T17:16:55Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T17:16:55Z","body":"Disabling safe save fixes it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160954762/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160961328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3160961328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3160961328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68aHEw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T17:19:21Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T17:19:21Z","body":"Then that's something to look into specifically for that, since symlinks are handled correctly otherwise, either this is because Godot fixes this itself, or because when opening the file directly instead of copying to it the behavior is different\n\nThis might be a question of how the file copy command is done, as it calls the kernel to do this","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160961328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160969279","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3160969279","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3160969279,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68aJA_","user":{"login":"aliaslion","id":122117018,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0dbmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122117018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion","html_url":"https://github.com/aliaslion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aliaslion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T17:22:28Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T17:22:28Z","body":"As far as I understand Godot renames the old file (the symlink), creates and writes a new file (not a symlink) and then deletes the old file. The only way I can see, to get around this, is to add specific behavior to Godot, so it detects the symlink and does safe save on the target file.\n\nThis will of course have to account for specific cases, like a symlink pointing to a symlink.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160969279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161006708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109364#issuecomment-3161006708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109364","id":3161006708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68aSJ0","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T17:34:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T17:34:32Z","body":"> As far as I understand Godot renames the old file (the symlink), creates and writes a new file (not a symlink) and then deletes the old file. The only way I can see, to get around this, is to add specific behavior to Godot, so it detects the symlink and does safe save on the target file.\n\nIt creates a temp file, writes to it and when it is closed replaces the original with it (using [rename](https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/rename.2.html)).\n\nI guess in case of symlink it should replace link target not link itself.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161006708/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]